      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T20:04:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since `get_usb_dev()` is documented as returning an iterable, not an iterator, this needs to be wrapper in `iter()` for correctness + safety.  Some iterable types are their own iterator, but not all (e.g. the builtin container types aren\u0027t, for example).\n\nIn other words make this:\n\n```\n    devs_iter \u003d iter(get_usb_dev(vidpid, serialname\u003dserialname))\n```\n\n(Yes name it `devs_iter` while at it, as a naming convention for having passed it through `iter()`.)",
      "revId": "3cf0a11253c56249ee7745598a5d93fcc262407d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
