      "writtenOn": "2023-09-05T20:04:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think using `None` instead of `bool` objects is a bit safer and more Pythonic.\n\nHow about:\n\n```\n    devs_iter \u003d iter(get_usb_dev(vidpid, serialname\u003dserialname))\n    first \u003d next(devs_iter, None)\n    if first is not None and next(devs_iter, None) is None:\n      return first.address\n    return None\n```",
      "revId": "3cf0a11253c56249ee7745598a5d93fcc262407d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
